    "intro": "<h3>Group Final Quiz 2 (with FRQ) — Instructions</h3><p>This is a <b>collaborative group test</b>. Work with your assigned group to discuss and solve each problem together. Every student must <b>submit their own answers individually</b> on their own device.</p><p><b>Topics covered (Weeks 7–13):</b></p><ul><li><b>Week 7 — Linear Programming: The Simplex Method (§4.1–4.2):</b> 2-variable max LP, 3-variable max LP, identify pivot column / pivot row / minimum ratio</li><li><b>Week 8:</b> Midterm — no new content on this quiz</li><li><b>Week 9 — Mathematics of Finance (§6.1–6.3):</b> Compound interest (annual vs monthly), ordinary annuity future value</li><li><b>Week 10 — Annuity and Amortization (§6.4):</b> Loan monthly payment and total interest</li><li><b>Week 11 — Intro to Sets (§7.1):</b> Set operations (union vs intersection); 2-circle Venn (exactly-one and neither)</li><li><b>Week 12 — Counting (§7.3, §7.5):</b> Permutations word problem, combinations with a required member, perm vs comb diagnostic</li><li><b>Week 13 — Intro to Probability (§8.1–8.2, §8.4):</b> 2x2 conditional probability + independence check, expected value E(X) and E(X²)</li></ul><p><b>Group work rules:</b></p><ul><li><b>Discuss first, submit individually.</b> Talk through each problem as a group before anyone submits.</li><li><b>Everyone participates.</b> Make sure every group member understands the reasoning before moving on.</li><li><b>Three attempts, no penalty.</b> You get 3 tries with the same version. Use them if your group wants to re-check a problem.</li><li><b>Stay with your group.</b> Do not leave the classroom or break off from your group until everyone has submitted.</li></ul><p>Your individual submission will be graded, but your score reflects your group's collective effort. Work together and make it count.</p>",
